# UI/UX change workflow — Pencil first, then code

Whenever there is a **change to how something looks, reads, or flows** on screen (UI, UX, layout, visuals, components, spacing, tablet/mobile behaviour, or screen structure) for Cosmos (prototypes or `src/public`), use **Pencil with strong UI/UX craft** so the design **matches the existing theme** and is **visibly excellent** — then **wait for the user to see and approve** before touching live code. **Do not** ship layout/visual work in the app in the same turn as the Pencil pass unless the user has **already approved** that design.

Personal skill (all projects): **`pencil-first-ui-ux`** in `~/.cursor/skills/pencil-first-ui-ux/SKILL.md`.

**MCP must be connected** for Agent design work — see **`pencil-mcp-setup.mdc`** and **`docs/dev/pencil-mcp-setup.md`**. `CallMcpTool` servers: **`user-highagency.pencildev-extension-pencil`** (editor open) or **`user-pencil`** (file on disk). Run **`npm run pencil:mcp-check`** if tools are missing.

**Component-level builds** (new or materially new UI surfaces): also follow **`component-build-md-pencil-then-db.mdc`** — companion **`.md` UI spec**, Pencil, **approval**, then app code and **only then** database/schema changes.

---

## 1. Update the design source (`.pen`)

- For non-trivial components, add or update a **Markdown UI spec** (e.g. `docs/ui/<feature>.md`) as described in **`component-build-md-pencil-then-db.mdc`**.
- **Single design source:** **`UIX/pencil-new.pen`** (all modules: Store OS, Store Pilot, Foundry, Command Unit, Army HR). Open this file in Pencil before MCP edits. Optionally mirror to **`src/public/design/pencil-local/pencil-new.pen`** after approval if that copy is still used locally.
- **Only** modify `.pen` files through the **Pencil MCP** (`batch_get`, `batch_design`, etc.) — do **not** edit `.pen` with Read/Write/grep. If MCP is unavailable, run **`npm run pencil:mcp-check`** and ask the user to enable MCP (do not silently skip to code unless waived).
- Follow **`.cursor/rules/pencil-mcp-no-notes.mdc`** — **never** add **`type: "note"`** documentation boxes on screens unless the user explicitly requests a note.
- Match the affected **screen/frame** to the real app (see `.cursor/rules/pencil-pos-url-mapping.mdc` for path labels on frames).
- In Pencil, mirror the **current design system**: blues/greens/surfaces consistent with existing frames, **legible type**, clear **primary vs secondary** actions, and **comfortable tap targets** — not wireframe placeholders unless the user asks for low-fi only.
- Apply **Cosmos UI polish** principles in the **implementation** phase (`ui-polish-rules.mdc`); in Pencil, aim for the same **hierarchy and density** the user asked for.

---

## 2. Pause for user approval

- After the `.pen` update, **do not** implement in HTML/CSS/JS in the **same turn** unless the user has **already approved** the design (this is **non-negotiable** for UI/UX changes).
- Ask the user to **approve** the Pencil change (e.g. review in Pencil, or request a **`get_screenshot`** / export of the relevant node if helpful).
- If they request tweaks, adjust **`.pen` first** again, then re-seek approval.

---

## 3. Implement in the actual app

**Only after approval:**

- Update the real files: e.g. `POS_Prototype.html`, `src/public/css/pos.css`, `src/public/css/lenskart-pos.css`, `src/public/js/pos.js`, etc.
- Follow **`.cursor/rules/ui-polish-rules.mdc`** (skeletons, toasts, `cosmosBtn*`, no raw “Loading…”, no `alert`, CSS variables, `.tr-link`, etc.).
- Keep parity with the **approved** Pencil layout; if code constraints differ, say so briefly and stay as close as possible.

---

## 4. Exceptions (narrow)

- **No visual or layout change** (e.g. fixing a JS error, API message, copy typo inside existing copy) → **Pencil step optional**; say you’re skipping Pencil and why.
- User explicitly says **to skip design** or **only change code** → follow their instruction.

---

## Checklist before marking UI work done

- [ ] `.pen` updated via Pencil MCP (or exception documented)
- [ ] User **approved** the design direction
- [ ] HTML/CSS/JS updated and aligned with approval
- [ ] UI polish rules satisfied
- [ ] `UIX/pencil-new.pen` updated; optional `pencil-local` mirror synced if used
